====================================================================================================
A. complete unit Cayley graphs over every imaginary quadratic field with |D| <= 2000, primes p <= 200
====================================================================================================
  fundamental discriminants scanned: 611 (class numbers 1..56; e.g. h histogram head [(1, 9), (2, 18), (3, 16), (4, 54), (5, 22), (6, 40)])
  complete unit Cayley graphs with N(P) >= 4:
    D = -3 (h = 1), p = 2 (inert), N(P) = 4  -> K4
    D = -3 (h = 1), p = 7 (split), N(P) = 7  -> K7
    D = -3 (h = 1), p = 7 (split), N(P) = 7  -> K7
    D = -4 (h = 1), p = 5 (split), N(P) = 5  -> K5
    D = -4 (h = 1), p = 5 (split), N(P) = 5  -> K5
  -> exactly (Q(sqrt-3), 4), (Q(i), 5) [both primes over 5], (Q(sqrt-3), 7) [both primes over 7]
  small-norm cases excluded by N(P) >= 4: every field gives K2 at N = 2 and K3 at N = 3 (units +-1 suffice)

